    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Each invoice now has an issue date and a due date, and both show on its row in the project's invoice table. `bin/e2e` passes. I also called the create API by hand: leaving the dates out fills them in, supplied dates are kept, and a due date before the issue date returns 400.\n\n**One thing in the test seed you should check.** The spec seeds the invoice with `status: 'SENT'`, but the app only has `UNPAID` and `PAID`, and the database rejects any other value. So the seed would fail. I didn't add a new \"sent\" status, since you didn't ask for one and it would affect the dashboard's outstanding total and the \"Mark paid\" button. Instead, the test-only seed endpoint (`TestSupportController`) stores `SENT` as `UNPAID`, which is what a sent but unpaid invoice is in this app. If you want \"sent\" as a real status, that's a separate change.\n\nWhat changed:\n- **Database:** a new migration, `V6__invoice_dates.sql`, adds `issued_date` and `due_date`, both required. Any existing invoices get today as the issue date and a due date 30 days later. The database also refuses a due date before the issue date.\n- **Server:** both dates are saved on the invoice and returned by the API as `yyyy-MM-dd`. When you create an invoice they're optional: the issue date defaults to today and the due date to 30 days after the issue date. The seed endpoint accepts `issuedDate` and `dueDate`.\n- **Front end:** the table has new \"Issued\" and \"Due\" columns with the test IDs the spec expects (`invoice-issued`, `invoice-due`). The add-invoice form has two optional date fields (`invoice-form-issued`, `invoice-form-due`) and shows an accessible error if the due date is before the issue date. No existing test IDs were changed.\n\nYour instructions said OfficeFloor, but the server is actually Spring Boot (only the package is named `net.officefloor`), so I wrote it as ordinary Spring code, as `CLAUDE.md` says.",
